 "response": "Likror's budget is now **$2632K**.\n\n1. **Authority:** Only Finance Office records change the budget. Every message from other teams is ignored, including all the \"heard\", \"expect\" and \"should land at\" claims.\n2. **Starting point:** #0001 sets the budget to $2090K.\n3. **Withdrawals:** I followed each withdrawal chain to its end. A withdrawal of a withdrawal brings the earlier item back, so an item counts if an even number of withdrawals sit above it. Some examples:\n   - #0279 withdraws #0113. That keeps #0022 in effect, which cancels #0021 and restores #0016. So #0013 (\u2212$268K) stays withdrawn.\n   - #0340 withdraws #0332. The chain then runs back through #0168, #0105, #0051 and #0027. The result is that #0003 (\u2212$82K) still applies.\n   - #1559 withdraws #1260, which keeps #1053 in effect. So #0384 (+$326K) is withdrawn.\n4. **Totals:**\n   - All Finance Office increases and decreases add up to a net \u2212$47K.\n   - The updates that end up withdrawn add up to a net \u2212$589K. Removing them changes the total by +$589K.\n   - Net effective change: \u2212$47K + $589K = +$542K.\n5. **Result:** $2090K + $542K = **$2632K**.\n\nThis was a single manual pass through the arithmetic. I did not recompute it independently, so a small addition error is possible.\n\nANSWER: $2632K",
